id: dead-zone
name: Dead Zone
uaType: magical
prerequisite: 2+ Skill Ranks in Use Magic
tpCost: 30
type: standard
actionCost: 3
kiCostPerBaseTier: 10
# Only its Actions, its Ki and its Might Clash are followed (the user's ruling). Open when used; "To maintain the
# existence of the Dead Zone portal, you must spend 1 Action and 5(T) Ki Points at the start of each of your turns" -
# paid on its own, a Stop on the card. The portal, the Dimension and the moving are the table's.
sustained: true
upkeepKiPerTier: 5
upkeepActions: 1
sphereMagnitude: minor
# "At the end of each of your turns, make a Might Clash against all Characters on the Battlefield" (combat.mjs).
pullsAtEnd: true
source: Core Rule
description: >
  A Minor Sphere portal to the Dead Zone: whoever enters it is sent there. At the end of each of your turns a Might Clash
  against everyone - losers move up to your Might toward it. 1 Action and 5(T) KP each turn keep it open.
text: >
  Dead Zone: You create a portal to the Dead Zone, sending whoever passes through to an eternal prison.
  –Ability Type: Magical
  –Prerequisites: 2+ Skill Ranks in Use Magic
  –TP Cost: 30
  –KP Cost: 10(bT)
  –Maneuver Type: Standard
  –Action Cost: 3 Actions
  –Minions: Non-Minion
  –Passive Bonus: N/A
  –Effect: You open the Dead Zone, creating a Minor Sphere AoE centered on an unoccupied Square within a Sphere AoE
  (centered on you) that has no Characters on an adjacent Square. This AoE is a portal into the Dead Zone, a Dimension
  (see — Dimensions) that can seal someone away within perpetual darkness. Any Character that enters a Square within the
  AoE created by this Unique Ability is immediately sent to the Dead Zone Dimension. If you are sent into the Dead Zone
  Dimension, the portal immediately closes.

  At the end of each of your turns, make a Might Clash against all Characters on the Battlefield. If they lose, they
  move a number of Squares up to your Might in the most direct path towards the Dead Zone portal.

  To maintain the existence of the Dead Zone portal, you must spend 1 Action and 5(T) Ki Points at the start of each of
  your turns. If you do not pay this cost, the portal to the Dead Zone will close.
